{
  "raw": {
    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Adjunct-Lecturer--Management_R0015076": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY The Management Division is currently accepting applications for adjunct faculty to teach strategy in our undergraduate and graduate programs. We are currently looking for faculty who can teach the core undergraduate strategy courses. The undergraduate core strategy course is a unique approach to teaching strategy as it bridges strategic frameworks, core concepts, and current business challenges using a unique issue-based problem-solving approach.   About the Management Division The Management Division is a team of innovative, collegial, and affable colleagues who are profoundly dedicated to their craft as educators, scholars, and practitioners. Our faculty includes award-winning teachers, thought leaders, and community leaders. They have educated and advised a wide variety of learners, from students to budding entrepreneurs to management and executives at Fortune 500 companies. Their research has been published in top-tier journals and has contributed knowledge to their discipline, to practice and to pedagogy. Finally, their leadership has made an impact on campus, in practice, and in the greater academy. More information about the Management Division can be found  here.   WHAT YOU WILL DO   Teach Management courses in our undergraduate and graduate programs. Take advantage of teaching development through our  Center for Engaged Teaching and Learning (CELT)  and coaching from colleagues. Obtain coaching and teaching support from colleagues. Assume additional responsibilities as required.    YOUR TEAM WILL INCLUDE N/A   WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED Relevant graduate degree (e.g., MBA, DBA, PhD) from an accredited university. Previous college or university teaching experience and/or practical Management experience relevant to the course(s) being taught. Alignment with our value of teaching excellence, collaboration, and inclusion, and those who embrace our mission to educate entrepreneurial leaders who create great economic and social value everywhere. Passionate for teaching strategy among an inclusive student community and developing your craft as a teacher, and for embracing new teaching innovations and technologies. Team-player mindset who is excited to coordinate and collaborate with other division faculty.   HOW AND WHERE YOU WILL WORK Babson College teaches courses in many different formats, including traditional semester schedules, intensive classroom experiences, evening classes, weekend classes, and on-line instruction. The rate for this position is $8,238 per course equivalency (CE). Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S.  Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role. APPLYING FOR THE POSITION Electronic applications should be submitted; no paper applications will be accepted. Please include: (1) a cover letter; (2) a current curriculum vitae; Candidates who advance in the application process will be asked to provide three reference letters."
    },
    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Adjunct-Lecturer--Marketing_R0015031": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Marketing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nPart time\n\nThe Marketing Division periodically seeks qualified applicants to serve as Adjunct Faculty to teach Marketing courses in our undergraduate and graduate programs.  Sample of courses: Principles of Marketing, Marketing Research, Marketing Analytics, Consumer Behavior, Brand Management, Customer Acquisition and Persuasion, Selling and Sales Management, Retailing Management, Social Media Marketing, Digital Marketing, Marketing Analytics, Developing Effective Advertising, Professional Sales Practicum, Marketing for Entrepreneurs, Sports Marketing, Strategic Marketing, Consumer Psychology, Pricing Strategy, Sales in Action, Marketing High Tech Products, Sales and Marketing Dynamics in Franchising, Sports and Brand Partnerships, AI-Enabled Selling for Customer Facing Financial Professionals, Business Storytelling, Engagement and Fundraising, Digital Analytics. As such, we accept applications on a rolling basis and review them when an opening becomes available. WHAT YOU WILL DO Teach courses in our undergraduate and graduate programs. Adjunct faculty have the opportunity to take advantage of teaching development through our Center for Engaged Teaching and Learning (CELT) and obtain coaching from colleagues. Assume additional responsibilities as required. WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED Relevant graduate degree (e.g., MBA, DBA, PhD) from an accredited university. Previous college or university teaching experience and/or practical Marketing experience relevant to the course(s) being taught. Alignment with our value of teaching excellence, collaboration, and inclusion, and those who embrace our mission to educate entrepreneurial leaders who create great economic and social value everywhere. Passion for teaching a range of students, for developing your craft as a teacher, and for embracing new teaching innovations and technologies. Team-player mindset who is excited to coordinate and collaborate with other faculty. HOW AND WHERE YOU WILL WORK Babson College teaches courses in many different formats, including traditional semester schedules, intensive classroom experiences, evening classes, weekend classes, and on-line instruction. The rate for this position in the Marketing Division is $8,238 per course equivalency (CE). Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S.  Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role."
    },
    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Assistant-Professor-in-Information-Systems_R0014901": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Information Systems",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY The Operations and Information Management Division at Babson College is seeking applicants for full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professors in Information Systems (including digital technologies and analytics) starting in the 2027-28 academic year. Our expectation is to hire at the Assistant level, but individuals with exceptional experience could be considered at the Associate level. We seek intellectually curious colleagues who are aligned with our mission of educating responsible entrepreneurial leaders who create economic and social value everywhere, and we are focused on attracting exceptional talent to add to the academic experience on our campus. About the Operations & Information Management Division   The Operations and Information Management (OIM) Division at Babson College is a community of collaborative, supportive colleagues, skilled at creative, experiential teaching methods. The OIM division comprises: (1) Eleven (11) academic professors with Ph.D. degrees and consulting experience who are accomplished researchers and exceptional teachers. Of the 11, 5 specialize in Information Systems (including data management, analytics, and digital transformation) and 6 specialize in Innovation and Operations Management. (2) Eight (8) professors of practice who have extensive industry connections (consulting and training) and (3) nine (9) adjunct professors who are practitioners in their respective fields. More information about the OIM division can be found at: Operations & Information Management | Babson College WHAT YOU WILL DO Teach a variety of topics in a core information systems course (including, at a foundational level, topics such as data management, IS design, AI/ML) at the undergraduate level delivered to an entrepreneurially focused, global, and multi-cultural student population in a business-focused school. Keenly interested in research with a proven track record of publications (or a strong pipeline of potential publications emerging from their doctoral program). Enthusiastic about teaching Babson’s undergraduate information systems core course Digital Technology for Entrepreneurs . This course is a broad survey of key and current topics in information systems. Interested in publishing in both academic and practitioner outlets (journals). Babson College emphasizes top-quality academic outlets. Babson College also encourages publications in top-quality practitioner outlets. Interested in developing a portfolio of materials (scholarly/practical) to contribute to broader academic communities and practice. Assume additional responsibilities as required. WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED A PhD and a background in business with strong technical skills in the application/use of AI/ML. Candidates with a degree in Computer Science are welcome to apply. Ideal candidates would be those who can teach our core undergraduate course and lead the division's efforts to develop a strong portfolio of technology courses focusing on AI/ML to keep us consistent with the industry demands. Works as a team player and is willing to collaborate with faculty within and across disciplines, both in integrated team teaching and in college service. Experienced with, and committed to, working in ways that will support and enhance the College’s commitment to teaching in an aligned, engaged, and inclusive manner. Willingness to embrace Babson’s unique approach to higher education Desire to invest in Babson’s success through active engagement in the campus community and as a helpful colleague. HOW AND WHERE YOU WILL WORK Ability to teach courses in-person, on-campus. The typical course load for a pre-tenure Assistant Professor position is four courses per year. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role. This is an exempt position with the following pay range: $170,795-$179,784. Interested candidates should submit: A cover letter. A CV detailing professional credentials and accomplishments in higher education and/or industry practice. A teaching statement detailing the candidate’s teaching philosophy and describing relevant teaching experiences and accomplishments. Where available, evidence of teaching quality, such as course evaluations and peer teaching observations, can be included as an appendix to the teaching statement. Full references will be solicited only upon application screening."
    },
    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Assistant-Teaching-Professor--Natural-Sciences_R0015025": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Natural Sciences",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY The Mathematics, Analytics, Science and Technology (MAST) Division at Babson College is seeking a full-time teaching professor in the natural sciences, with an environmental science focus. The position is non-tenure track, at the Assistant level and the start date is Fall 2027. A successful applicant will have a passion for undergraduate teaching of non-science majors, as Babson only confers business degrees. The successful applicant will also be active in some form of research or applied work, whether traditional discipline-specific research, pedagogical research or interdisciplinary research or applications. Finally, a successful applicant will also demonstrate a desire to contribute to Babson’s mission through service on campus. The MAST Division includes nineteen full-time faculty and several part-time instructors. WHAT YOU WILL DO Teach natural science to undergraduates. Teaching responsibilities will vary and may include the foundation science courses (multi-science discipline courses with hands-on labs) and our innovative intermediate Socio-Ecological Systems courses , which pair a natural scientist with a social scientist to co-teach integrated sustainability and systems thinking. Work as a team player and willing to collaborate with faculty across disciplines, both in integrated team teaching and in college service.   Commit to working in ways that will support and enhance the College’s commitment to teaching in an aligned, engaged, and inclusive manner. Assume additional responsibilities as required. WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED Ph.D. (or an equivalent terminal degree) in a natural science discipline with a strong connection to environmental science, climate science, ecology, environmental studies, and/or energy systems.  We encourage applications from faculty of all backgrounds and career stages. Passionate about teaching and innovative curriculum development in the undergraduate setting. Demonstrated competency in traditional academic research, scholarship of teaching and learning, or engagement in practice. A team player, willing to lead and collaborate with faculty from multiple disciplines to co-design and co-teach courses in an integrated, cross-disciplinary context. Aligned with our values of teaching excellence, collaboration, and inclusion. Embraces Babson’s mission to educate entrepreneurial leaders who create great economic and social value everywhere. HOW AND WHERE YOU WILL WORK Ability to teach courses in-person, on-campus. We encourage and support professional development by providing manageable teaching loads (six face-to-face sections per year for all ranks, generally evenly split across Fall and Spring semesters; additionally, the goal is for 1-2 individual course preparations/semester), small class sizes, excellent technological support, and research or travel funding. We have limited science lab research space, but value collaboration across disciplines and between institutions. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role. This is an exempt position with the following pay range: $74,645 - $78,573 We are posting at the Teaching Assistant Professor level. However, we encourage candidates whose credentials and experience may align more closely with a different faculty rank to apply, as their qualifications will be considered during the review process. Please include: (1) a cover letter; (2) a current curriculum vitae; (3) a brief (1-2 page) teaching philosophy, including a short statement on inclusive excellence in the classroom; (4) a brief (1-2 page) professional development or research statement discussing prior work, future plans and required support. (4) Candidates who advance in the application process will be asked to provide three reference letters. Application Materials will be reviewed starting on November 1st and continue on a rolling basis during the Fall semester."
    },
    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Adjunct-Lecturer--Finance_R0015028": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Finance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nPart time\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY The Finance Division periodically seeks qualified applicants to serve as Adjunct Faculty to teach Finance courses in our undergraduate and graduate programs. As such, we accept applications on a rolling basis and review them when an opening becomes available. About the Finance Division The Finance Division is a team of innovative, collegial, and affable colleagues who are profoundly dedicated to their craft as educators, scholars, and practitioners. Our faculty include award-winning teachers, thought leaders, and community leaders. They have educated and advised a wide variety of learners, from students to budding entrepreneurs to management and executives at Fortune 500 companies. Their research has been published in top-tier journals and has contributed knowledge to their discipline, to practice and to pedagogy. Finally, their leadership has made an impact on campus, in practice, and in the greater academy.  More information about the Finance Division can be found  here .  WHAT YOU WILL DO Teach Finance courses in our undergraduate and graduate programs. Take advantage of teaching development through our  Center for Engaged Teaching and Learning (CELT)  and coaching from colleagues. Assume additional responsibilities as required. WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED Relevant graduate degree (e.g., MBA, DBA, PhD) from an accredited university. Previous college or university teaching experience and/or practical Finance experience relevant to the course(s) being taught. Alignment with our value of teaching excellence, collaboration, and inclusion, and those who embrace our mission to educate entrepreneurial leaders who create great economic and social value everywhere. Passion for teaching a range of students, for developing your craft as a teacher, and for embracing new teaching innovations and technologies. Team-player mindset who is excited to coordinate and collaborate with other faculty. HOW AND WHERE YOU WILL WORK Babson College teaches courses in many different formats, including traditional semester schedules, intensive classroom experiences, evening classes, weekend classes, and on-line instruction. The rate for this position is $8,238 per course equivalency (CE). Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role."
    },
    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Lab-Instructor--Adjunct_R0014926": {
      "title": "Lab Instructor, Adjunct",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nPart time\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY The lab instructor position is responsible for working with students during NST1 lab sections during the semester that course is taught. WHAT YOU WILL DO Familiar with the overall lab structure; may meet with the faculty or science director prior to each lab section as part of the preparation work. During class time, may outline the overall goal of the lab, demonstrate how the individual pieces of lab equipment work, and manage common lab materials. Collect all lab results and take down or put together the lab setup for the next class. Once lab reports are submitted, grade all assignments and enters the results into the Canvas LMS. Assume additional responsibilities as required. YOUR TEAM WILL INCLUDE N/A WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED Relevant Master’s Degree from an accredited university. Previous teaching experience and/or work/practical experience in the natural sciences. Alignment with our values of teaching excellence, collaboration, and inclusion, and those who embrace our mission to educate entrepreneurial leaders who create great economic and social value everywhere. Team-player mindset who is excited to coordinate and collaborate with others. HOW AND WHERE YOU WILL WORK Babson College teaches courses in many different formats, including traditional semester schedules, intensive classroom experiences, evening classes, weekend classes, and online instruction. The rate for this position in the Mathematics, Analytics, Science, and Technology Division is 1/3 CE for each lab section which is $2,528.66 per lab section. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S.  Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role."
    },
