      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Tech, Ops & Information Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nPart time\n\nTHE OPPORTUNITY The Operations & Information Management Division periodically seeks qualified applicants to serve as Adjunct Faculty to teach Operations and Information Management courses in our undergraduate and graduate programs. As such, we accept applications on a rolling basis and review them when an opening becomes available. WHAT YOU WILL DO Teach courses in our undergraduate and graduate programs (Babson College teaches courses in many different formats, including traditional semester schedules, intensive classroom experiences, evening classes, weekend classes, and online instruction). Adjunct faculty have the opportunity to take advantage of teaching development through our Center for Engaged Teaching and Learning (CELT) and obtain coaching from colleagues. Assume additional responsibilities as required. YOUR TEAM WILL INCLUDE N/A WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED Relevant graduate degree (e.g., MBA, DBA, PhD) from an accredited university. Previous college or university teaching experience and/or work/practical experience in the management of information systems. Alignment with our values of teaching excellence, collaboration, and inclusion, and those who embrace our mission to educate entrepreneurial leaders who create great economic and social value everywhere. Passion for teaching a range of students, for developing your craft as a teacher, and for embracing new teaching innovations and technologies. Team-player mindset who is excited to coordinate and collaborate with other faculty. HOW AND WHERE YOU WILL WORK Babson College teaches courses in many different formats, including traditional semester schedules, intensive classroom experiences, evening classes, weekend classes, and online instruction. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S.  Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role. The rate for this position in the Operations & Information Management Division is $8,238 per course equivalency (CE)."
    },
    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Adjunct-Lecturer--Business-Law_R0014899-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Business Law",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-21\nPart time\n\nThe Accounting & Law Division periodically seeks qualified applicants to serve as Adjunct Faculty to teach Law courses in our undergraduate and graduate programs. As such, we accept applications on a rolling basis and review them when an opening becomes available. About the Accounting & Law Division The Accounting & Law Division is a team of innovative, collegial, and affable colleagues who are profoundly dedicated to their craft as educators, scholars, and practitioners. Our faculty include award-winning teachers, thought leaders and community leaders. They have educated and advised a wide variety of learners, from students to budding entrepreneurs to management and executives at fortune 500 companies. Their research has been published in top-tier journals and have contributed knowledge to their discipline, to practice and to pedagogy. Finally, their leadership has made an impact on campus, in practice, and in the greater academy. More information about the Accounting & Law Division can be found here . WHAT YOU WILL DO Teach Business Law courses in our undergraduate and graduate programs. Take advantage of teaching development through our  Center for Engaged Teaching and Learning (CELT)  and coaching from colleagues. Assume additional responsibilities as required. WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED Relevant graduate degree (e.g., JD, LLB, LLM) from an accredited university and is professionally licensed. Previous college or university teaching experience and/or practical law experience relevant to the course(s) being taught. Alignment with our value of teaching excellence, collaboration, and inclusion, and those who embrace our mission to educate entrepreneurial leaders who create great economic and social value everywhere. Passion for teaching a range of students, for developing your craft as a teacher, and for embracing new teaching innovations and technologies. Team-player mindset who is excited to coordinate and collaborate with other faculty. HOW AND WHERE YOU WILL WORK Babson College teaches courses in many different formats, including traditional semester schedules, intensive classroom experiences, evening classes, weekend classes, and on-line instruction. The rate for this position is $8,238 per course equivalency (CE). Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role."
    },
