    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Adjunct-Lecturer--Accounting_R0014806-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Accounting",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-08\nPart time\n\nThe Accounting & Law Division periodically seeks qualified applicants to serve as Adjunct Faculty to teach accounting courses in our undergraduate and graduate programs. As such, we accept applications on a rolling basis and review them when an opening becomes available. The Accounting   &   Law Division   is a team of innovative, collegial, and affable colleagues who are profoundly dedicated to their craft as educators, scholars, and practitioners. Our faculty   include   award-winning teachers, thought   leaders   and community leaders. They have educated and   advised   a wide variety of learners, from students to budding entrepreneurs to management and executives at fortune 500 companies. Their research has been published in top-tier journals and   have   contributed knowledge to their discipline, to practice and to pedagogy. Finally, their leadership has made an impact on campus, in practice, and in the greater academy.   More information about the   Accounting & Law Division   can be found   here .   What you will do: Teach   accounting   courses in our undergraduate and graduate programs.   Take advantage of teaching development through our  Center for Engaged Teaching and Learning (CELT)  and coaching from colleagues.   Assume   additional   responsibilities as   required .   Education and Skills you will need: Relevant graduate degree (e.g., MBA,   MSA,   DBA, PhD) from an accredited university   and preferably one or more professional certifications (e.g., CPA, CMA).     Previous   college or university teaching experience and/or practical   accounting   experience relevant to the course ( s )   being taught.   Alignment with our value of teaching excellence, collaboration, and inclusion, and those who embrace our mission to educate entrepreneurial leaders who create great economic and social value everywhere.   Passion for teaching a range of students, for developing your craft as a teacher, and for embracing new teaching innovations and technologies.   Team-player mindset who is excited to coordinate and collaborate with other faculty.   Babson College teaches courses in many different formats, including traditional semester schedules, intensive classroom experiences, evening classes, weekend classes, and on-line instruction.     The rate for this position is  $8,238   per   course   equivalency (CE).     Applicants must   be authorized to   work for any employer in the U.S. Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role."
    },
    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Adjunct-Lecturer--Arts---Humanities_R0014702": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Arts & Humanities",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-04\nPart time\n\nThe Arts & Humanities Division accepts applications from qualified applicants for adjunct faculty positions and reviews them when an opening becomes available. The 40+ faculty in the Arts & Humanities Division teach core and elective courses in the undergraduate program across a wide range of disciplines and liberal arts specializations. Babson College is an independent school of management that takes an innovative approach to prepare undergraduates, graduate students, and working professionals for the challenges of the modern business world. Babson undergraduate students take approximately half of their credits in the liberal arts. Babson’s unique curriculum focuses on developing critical thinking and a wide range of multidimensional skills that prepare Babson graduates to make important contributions to business and society in dynamic environments. WHAT YOU WILL DO Teach liberal arts courses in our undergraduate program for the Arts & Humanities Division .   Take advantage of teaching development through our  Center for Engaged Teaching and Learning (CELT)  and coaching from colleagues. Assume additional responsibilities as required. WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED Relevant graduate degree (e.g., MFA, PhD) from an accredited university. M.A. or MFA for Writing areas; M.A. in a related field for the other scholarly disciplines. College teaching experience required for all positions. Applicants may also be ABD or hold a PhD in the appropriate field. Previous college or university teaching experience and/or practical disciplinary/field experience relevant to the course(s) being taught. Alignment with our value of teaching excellence, collaboration, and inclusion, and those who embrace our mission to educate entrepreneurial leaders who create great economic and social value everywhere. Passion for teaching a range of students, for developing your craft as a teacher, and for embracing new teaching innovations and technologies. Team-player mindset who is excited to coordinate and collaborate with other faculty. This position requires the ability to teach courses in-person, on-campus. The rate for this position is $7,437 per course equivalency (CE). Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role."
    },
    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Adjunct-Lecturer---History---Society-Division_R0014696": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer,  History & Society Division",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-04\nPart time\n\nThe History & Society Division accepts applications from qualified applicants for adjunct faculty positions and reviews them when an opening becomes available. WHAT YOU WILL DO Teach courses in our undergraduate programs. Adjunct faculty have the opportunity to take advantage of teaching development through our Center for Engaged Teaching and Learning (CELT) and obtain coaching from colleagues. Assume additional responsibilities as required. WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED Requires an ABD in an appropriate Social Science discipline, and college teaching experience. This position is well-suited for an advanced graduate student seeking teaching experience in preparation for entering the faculty job market. Must be aligned with our values of teaching excellence, collaboration, and inclusion, and those who embrace our mission to educate entrepreneurial leaders who create great economic and social value everywhere. Demonstrate a passion for teaching a range of students, be collaborative team-players, be willing to learn and adapt teaching technology, and have experience that can quickly establish credibility in the classroom. Is a team player, excited to coordinate teaching with other faculty in the division. HOW AND WHERE YOU WILL WORK Courses will usually be in-person on Babson’s Wellesley campus during regular semesters and will meet for 90 minutes twice a week on Monday and Wednesday, or Tuesday and Thursday. The rate for this position is $7,437 per course equivalency (CE). Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S.  Babson does not sponsor for employment-based petitions/applications for this role."
    },
    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Adjunct-Lecturer--Writing_R0014703": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Writing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-27\nPart time\n\nThe Arts and Humanities Division at Babson College has openings for an Adjunct Instructor of Writing for the Spring 2026 semester. The College’s Writing Program consists of a two-course sequence emphasizing writing across contexts. The instructor will teach up to three sections of either Writing Across Contexts (WRT1001) or Research Writing (WRT2000). Babson College is an independent school of management that takes an innovative approach to prepare undergraduates, graduate students, and working professionals for the challenges of the modern business world. Babson undergraduate students take approximately half of their credits in the liberal arts. Babson’s unique curriculum focuses on developing critical thinking and a wide range of multidimensional skills that prepare Babson graduates to make important contributions to business and society in dynamic environments. WHAT YOU WILL DO Teach writing courses in our undergraduate program. Take advantage of teaching development through our  Center for Engaged Teaching and Learning (CELT)  and coaching from colleagues. Assume additional responsibilities as required. WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED A master’s degree and experience teaching college-level first-year composition are required. Alignment with our value of teaching excellence, collaboration, and inclusion, and those who embrace our mission to educate entrepreneurial leaders who create great economic and social value everywhere. Passion for teaching a range of students, for developing your craft as a teacher, and for embracing new teaching innovations and technologies. Team-player mindset who is excited to coordinate and collaborate with other faculty. HOW AND WHERE YOU WILL WORK This position requires the ability to teach courses in-person, on-campus.   The rate for this position in the Arts & Humanities Division is $7437 per course equivalency (CE). Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S. Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role."
    },
    "https://babson.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Faculty/job/Wellesley-MA/Speech-Consultant_R0015075": {
      "title": "Speech Consultant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nThe Speech Consultant meets at designated times with graduate and undergraduate students, faculty, staff, alum and other participants of Babson programs. The Speech Consultant will instruct on communication assignments, train on speech techniques, tutor for presentation improvement, and provide overall coaching on specific styles of presentations and many communication-related topics. Sessions are one-one, small group, and class instruction. WHAT YOU WILL DO Participate in specific classes for developing individual and group presentation skills, creating personal brands, developing confidence, building interpersonal skills, and improving online communication strategies.  Performs one-on-one coaching/tutoring, delivers classroom lectures, creates and delivers various workshops, and assists faculty/staff, and special programs on new services. Confirms student attendance, follows-up with students, attends meetings on various requirements for different programs, meets with other professors for their classroom needs, creates new lectures for classroom visits and attends quarterly Speech Consultant team meetings.  Optional: Attend college events including sports games, workshops, seminars, and other community events.  Assume additional responsibilities as required. YOUR TEAM WILL INCLUDE N/A   WHAT EDUCATION AND SKILLS YOU WILL NEED Requires a master’s degree, preferably a PhD or EDD, 2-3 years of college teaching experience and/or equivalent with business communication coaching experience.  Envision and propose new methods to perform tasks that support ET&A; take thoughtful risks; and accept new and ongoing initiatives, objectives, and solutions to gain sought-after results. Ability to anticipate and embrace change; demonstrate willingness to achieve, acquire, and utilize new skills and challenging tasks; and is flexible in changing conditions. Must be flexible and willing to assume new tasks.   HOW AND WHERE YOU WILL WORK Positions are temporary by semester; hours and length of assignment may vary, including nights and weekends.  The pay rate for this position is as follows: 52 hours in a semester would be $4,119; 104 hours in a semester would be $8,238. Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the U.S.  Babson does not sponsor employment-based petitions/applications for this role. APPLYING FOR THE POSITION Electronic applications should be submitted; no paper applications will be accepted. Please include: (1) a cover letter; (2) a current curriculum vitae; Candidates who advance in the application process will be asked to provide three reference letters."
    }
  },
